Description: Read the partition to replace before reverting the device
 In "Replace a partition", ChoicePage::doReplaceSelectedPartition() hands the
 preview view's QModelIndex to a worker thread, which first reverts the device
 when an earlier choice changed it (revertDevice) and only then reads the
 partition through the index: its path, or, for free space, the Partition*
 behind PartitionPtrRole and that partition's sectors and parent. Reverting the
 device makes the page rebuild its preview views, whose model owns the index, so
 the worker read a dangling index. Confirming the encryption passphrase after a
 partition had been selected runs exactly that path (onEncryptWidgetStateChanged
 calls doReplaceSelectedPartition with the current index of a page whose device
 the selection had changed), and Calamares crashed; selecting encryption first
 did not, because nothing had changed the device yet. Seen installing Oaxaca on
 a Lenovo Legion Pro 7 on 2026-10-12, with free space selected. The same family
 as Calamares issue 2535 ("Segfault in QStandardItemModel::flags() when
 changing selection in Replace a partition mode", open).
 .
 The patch reads the path, the free-space flag, the first and last sector and
 the extended parent's path from the index on the GUI thread, before the worker
 starts, and the worker uses only those values.
Author: santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>
Origin: vendor
Bug: https://codeberg.org/Calamares/calamares/issues/2535
